## 3. Free 30-Day Evaluation License

Commercial organizations may request a **free 30-day evaluation license** for the purpose of testing and evaluating SentinelCore.

An evaluation license is granted only when explicitly approved in writing by ARASAKA CORP.

The evaluation license may permit the requesting organization to:

* install SentinelCore on evaluation systems;
* run SentinelCore in a test, development, laboratory, or limited production environment;
* evaluate its security features and functionality;
* evaluate performance, compatibility, detection capabilities, and operational suitability;
* integrate SentinelCore with internal systems solely for evaluation purposes;
* provide reasonable feedback to ARASAKA CORP regarding the evaluation.

The evaluation period begins on the date specified in the written evaluation approval and expires automatically after **30 calendar days**, unless ARASAKA CORP agrees in writing to extend the evaluation period.

The evaluation license is:

* free of charge;
* non-transferable;
* non-sublicensable;
* limited to the organization named in the written approval;
* limited to the number of installations, users, systems, or other conditions specified in the written approval.

The evaluation license does not grant the organization a continuing right to commercially use SentinelCore after the evaluation period expires.

After the evaluation period ends, the organization must either:

1. obtain an appropriate commercial license from ARASAKA CORP; or
2. stop using SentinelCore and delete or disable its evaluation installations and copies, except where retention is required by law.

An evaluation license does not automatically convert into a commercial license.

## 4. Requesting an Evaluation License

Organizations wishing to evaluate SentinelCore may request a 30-day evaluation license by contacting:

**ARASAKA CORP**
[void@arasaka-corp.eu](mailto:void@arasaka-corp.eu)

Evaluation requests may include:

* organization name;
* intended use;
* number of systems or installations;
* operating systems;
* expected evaluation period;
* technical contact;
* any other information reasonably required to determine the appropriate evaluation terms.

ARASAKA CORP may approve, deny, or impose additional conditions on an evaluation license at its discretion.

No evaluation license exists unless it has been explicitly granted in writing by an authorized representative of ARASAKA CORP.

